#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:169
#: ff7b2285e22c4bb88917562d97d08bea
msgid "5. PO Syntax, Header, Charset, and Fuzzy Flag Preservation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:171
#: 4586fafd95a9472b91fe873c5e39a7be
msgid ""
"To ensure `msgfmt`, `pybabel`, and Hatchling packaging "
"(`tools/hatch_build.py`) never fail during wheel or sdist builds, the "
"translation workflow enforces five `.po` syntax invariants:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:174
#: ad1e4fc7ce044096b5c9558f04b53df4
msgid ""
"**Header Metadata & `UTF-8` Charset Declaration**: The root `msgid \"\"` "
"header block (`Project-Id-Version`, `MIME-Version: 1.0`, `Content-Type: "
"text/plain; charset=utf-8`, `Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit`) is parsed "
"separately and never sent to the translation backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:178
#: 2285757afa224945b28f109d65206953
msgid ""
"**Plural-Forms Header Expression Awareness**: The translator reads the "
"target locale's `nplurals=N` header (for example, `nplurals=1` for `ja`, "
"`nplurals=2` for `de`/`es`/`fr`, `nplurals=3` for `ru`/`pl`, and "
"`nplurals=6` for `ar`) and requests exactly `N` plural forms for every "
"`msgid_plural` entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:182
#: d9eb180cd94f4050b6508d65751439e1
msgid ""
"**Multiline String Wrapping**: Multiline `msgid` blocks (such as CLI "
"`Examples:` and `Environment Variables:` help sections) preserve exact "
"`\\n` line-break counts and column indentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:185
#: 68597c127c574fba9776a28c5d84651a
msgid ""
"**Fuzzy Flag (`#, fuzzy`) Lifecycle**: Entries marked `#, fuzzy` by "
"`msgmerge` / `pybabel update` can be targeted for re-translation; once "
"validated by `validate_message_pair()`, the `#, fuzzy` flag is cleared "
"and an attribution comment (`# AI-translated: <model>`) is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:188
#: dbcd9dbc50ae47c796d134f40d0b1164
msgid ""
"**Relative Source Location Hygiene**: Every catalog write invokes "
"`_sanitize_po_locations()` from `tools/i18n.py` so `#: src/findfmt/...` "
"comments never leak absolute developer filesystem paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:193
#: 819128e4a13c4aaeadb211f72c45e44f
msgid "6. Failure Modes, Rate Limiting, and Partial Batch Resume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 097650707ae843a18817e28ce87db3d4
msgid "Failure Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: c91be8593b9d43308d5bbefe92cf5a85
msgid "Mitigation Strategy in `findfmt` Translation Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 4e3480a314b04067b213592adceaa874
msgid "**HTTP `429` Rate Limiting / `5xx` Timeouts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: ceafb70b72e548c0bb8d8a623233d802
msgid ""
"Exponential backoff with jitter (`base=1.5s`, `max_retries=4`, respecting"
" `Retry-After` headers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 9855af574f3a424692b8779c84bd5ae7
msgid "**Mid-Catalog Network Interruption**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 07a8969310de41858ba697cbd1cb2ed7
msgid ""
"Deterministic batch checkpointing: each completed batch of 25 strings is "
"flushed to disk or cache so re-running resumes only untranslated items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 5fbed9a2362540d09143ec499a11407c
msgid "**Dropped or Mutated `__PH_N__` Token**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 0f370afb2f1447faa6e1ab2a4058ac10
msgid ""
"`unmask_placeholders()` raises `ValueError` immediately; the single "
"offending entry is retried in isolation or left untranslated with a "
"warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 3c2551a970df4daea4333c2a1cd9a364
msgid "**Malformed Plural Array Length**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 28f539255fd74ac9b86a729512fddd10
msgid ""
"Verified against `nplurals` in the `.po` header before writing "
"`msgstr[0..N-1]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: 4d2ac5749759489ea1e162c6c7346a8b
msgid "**Compile-Time Gate (`tools/i18n.py`)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:160
#: a7c2275a98444e62afabd0a4dc98af4f
msgid ""
"`tools/i18n.py validate` and `tools/i18n.py compile` block `.mo` "
"compilation if any entry fails placeholder or Rich markup parity checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:205
#: ac60e3567e4f46fbaf8150a72ea79c39
msgid "7. Domain Prompt Engineering, Technical Glossary, and Pluralization Rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/ai_translation_benchmark.md:207
#: 95b6305d05c54574896e0b1eef92aa46
msgid ""
"Generic machine translation often mistranslates specialized CLI terms "
"(`shebang`, `pruning`, `glob`, `symlink`, `MIME tag`, `pager`) or "
"corrupts CLI flags (`--format`, `-t`). `tools/i18n_prompts.py` defines "
"the reusable prompt templates, authoritative terminology glossary, and "
"`ngettext` pluralization rules consumed by the translation pipeline "
"(Issue [#305](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/issues/305))."
